 I was playing an Elf today (for the first time in months), and thought
of a change that could be made to the game to make missile weapons more
realistic and useful. Instead of 't'hrowing arrows at your enemies, use
an aiming type of input, like in Ultima V. This would let you fire at
creatures that aren't directly in line or diagonal from you. Perhaps use
the same code that's used for '/' identifying things. Also, if you miss,
you might have a chance of hitting a creature in a neighborring square.
 Also, the same type of aiming could be used for 't'hrowing, and use 'f'
for 'f'ire weapon in hand. Ah well, just some random thoughts...

